        "id": "flask/testing.py::class::EnvironBuilder::642::s0",
        "kind": "class",
        "explain": "Subclass of werkzeug.test.EnvironBuilder that builds WSGI environments using defaults taken from a Flask application. Its constructor enforces mutual exclusion between base_url and the subdomain/url_scheme shortcuts, derives a base URL from app config when none is supplied (parsing path as a possible absolute URL), and overrides JSON serialization to use the app's JSON provider. Members __init__ and json_dumps are fully explained here.",
        "summary": "EnvironBuilder taking environment defaults from a Flask app.",
        "members": [
          "flask/testing.py::method::EnvironBuilder.__init__::1667",
          "flask/testing.py::method::EnvironBuilder.json_dumps::2850"
        ],
        "relations": [
          {
            "target": "werkzeug.test.EnvironBuilder",
            "kind": "inherit",
            "basis": "class EnvironBuilder(werkzeug.test.EnvironBuilder)"
          }
        ],
        "uncertainties": [
          "Validation performed by the werkzeug base constructor is outside the supplied source."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "flask/testing.py::method::EnvironBuilder.__init__::1667",
        "kind": "method",
        "explain": "Initializes the builder for a request to app. An assert enforces the argument contract: subdomain or url_scheme may only be passed without base_url (mutually exclusive); failure raises AssertionError, stripped under python -O. When base_url is None, the host comes from config SERVER_NAME (fallback 'localhost'), app root from config APPLICATION_ROOT, scheme from explicit url_scheme or config PREFERRED_URL_SCHEME. path may be a full URL; urlsplit lets an explicit scheme/netloc in path override the derived values, the subdomain prefixes the host, and the query string is reattached to the path. Resulting base_url is scheme://host/<app root, leading slash stripped>. The app is stored on self.app before delegating to the werkzeug base constructor with remaining positional/keyword arguments, which handles body, headers, JSON, etc.",
        "summary": "Builds a request environment, deriving base URL and defaults from app config.",
        "extras": [
          {
            "topic": "contract",
            "note": "Requires app config keys SERVER_NAME, APPLICATION_ROOT, and PREFERRED_URL_SCHEME; only SERVER_NAME has a fallback."
          }
        ],
        "relations": [
          {
            "target": "werkzeug.test.EnvironBuilder",
            "kind": "call",
            "basis": "super().__init__(path, base_url, *args, **kwargs)"
          }
        ],
        "uncertainties": [
          "Behavior of urlsplit on path values without scheme/netloc is standard urllib behavior assumed, not verified here."
        ]
      }
